// Issue-validation golden set. One case per line: { id, tags, input: { title, body }, expected: { valid, score_min?, score_max? } }.
// Lines starting with // are comments. Labels follow prompts/validation-system.md (B1–B4 blockers, score >= 70).
// Only cases the LLM judges: deterministic guards (e.g. a tag-only title, short-circuited by isMeaningfulTitle) are unit-tested, not evaluated.
{"id":"valid-api-endpoint","tags":["valid","api"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add GET /health endpoint","body":"## Context\nAdd a health endpoint to `src/server.mjs` (Express app).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GET /health` returns HTTP 200 with JSON body `{ \"status\": \"ok\" }`\n- [ ] Response has `Content-Type: application/json`\n- [ ] `POST /health` returns HTTP 405\n- [ ] A test in `test/health.test.mjs` covers both cases\n\n## Out of scope\nDependency checks (DB, cache)."},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-pure-function","tags":["valid","lib"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add slugify helper","body":"Add `slugify(text)` to `scripts/lib/strings.mjs`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `slugify('Hello World')` returns `'hello-world'`\n- [ ] Consecutive non-alphanumeric characters collapse to one `-`\n- [ ] Leading/trailing `-` are trimmed\n- [ ] `slugify('')` returns `''`\n- [ ] `slugify(null)` throws `TypeError`\n- [ ] Unit tests in `scripts/tests/strings.test.mjs` cover each item"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-bugfix","tags":["valid","bug"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] parseFlatYaml drops values containing a colon","body":"## Bug\n`parseFlatYaml` in `scripts/lib/yaml.mjs` splits on every `:`, so `url: https://x.dev` parses as `https`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `parseFlatYaml('url: https://x.dev')` returns `{ url: 'https://x.dev' }`\n- [ ] Keys without a value still parse to `''`\n- [ ] Existing tests in `scripts/tests/yaml.test.mjs` still pass\n- [ ] A regression test covers the colon-in-value case"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-docs-diagram","tags":["valid","docs"],"input":{"title":"[DOCS] Add pipeline Mermaid diagram to README","body":"Add a Mermaid flowchart to `README.md` under a new `## Pipeline` section.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `README.md` contains a `## Pipeline` section with a ```mermaid block\n- [ ] The diagram has nodes labeled Issue Validation, Code Generation, PR Review, Auto-fix, Human Merge\n- [ ] Directed edges connect them in that order, plus Auto-fix → PR Review\n- [ ] No other README section is modified\n\nGitHub renders Mermaid natively; no tooling required."},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-config-change","tags":["valid","config"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Raise validation_max_tokens to 1536","body":"## Change\nIn `config/models.yaml`, set `validation_max_tokens: 1536` (currently 1024) because reasoning tokens truncate the JSON output.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `config/models.yaml` has `validation_max_tokens:  1536`\n- [ ] `loadLLMConfig('validation').maxTokens === 1536` (assert in `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs`)\n- [ ] No other key in `config/models.yaml` changes"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-error-handling","tags":["valid","edge"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] readCheckpoint returns null on corrupt JSON","body":"`readCheckpoint` in `scripts/lib/checkpoint.mjs` currently throws on a corrupt checkpoint file.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] When the file contains invalid JSON, `readCheckpoint` returns `null`\n- [ ] When the file is missing, it still returns `null`\n- [ ] When the file is valid, the parsed object is returned unchanged\n- [ ] A warning is logged via `logger.error` with the file path on corrupt JSON\n- [ ] Tests cover all three cases"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"invalid-no-ac","tags":["invalid","b1"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add dark mode","body":"Users want dark mode. Please add it."},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-vague-ac","tags":["invalid","b1"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] Login is broken","body":"Login doesn't work sometimes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fix the bug\n- [ ] It should work correctly"},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-subjective-ac","tags":["invalid","b2"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Redesign settings page","body":"Redesign `src/pages/Settings.tsx`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The page looks modern and clean\n- [ ] Users find it intuitive\n- [ ] It feels responsive"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-unmeasurable-perf","tags":["invalid","b2"],"input":{"title":"[PERF] Speed up PR review","body":"`scripts/pr_review.mjs` is slow.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Review should be faster\n- [ ] Better performance overall"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-ambiguous-scope","tags":["invalid","b3"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add caching","body":"We should cache things to reduce load.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Responses are cached\n- [ ] Cache hit returns the cached value"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-arch-choice","tags":["invalid","b3"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Persist pipeline metrics","body":"Metrics should be stored somewhere durable, either Postgres or Redis, whatever fits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Metrics survive a restart\n- [ ] Metrics can be queried"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-undocumented-dependency","tags":["invalid","b4"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Post review summary to Slack","body":"After each review, send the verdict to Slack through the notifier service the platform team is building. It is not deployed yet and has no published endpoint or API contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pr_review.mjs` calls the notifier with `{ prNumber, verdict }`\n- [ ] A Slack message appears in #dev-loop"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-empty-body","tags":["invalid","b1","edge"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Improve logging","body":""},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-problem-only","tags":["invalid","b1"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] Auto-fix loops forever on PR #42","body":"On PR #42 the auto-fix workflow kept pushing commits for an hour. Logs attached in the run. Something is wrong with the attempt counter in `scripts/auto_fix_pr.mjs`."},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// --- Discriminating edge cases (30-case set). Tags: partial-ac, role-scope, stub, short, fr, warnings-only. ---
// B2 "BLOCKED when any AC item is subjective": one subjective item among four testable ones is enough.
{"id":"invalid-partial-ac-subjective","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Validate config/labels.yaml on load","body":"`loadLabels()` in `scripts/lib/config.mjs` accepts any YAML today.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A label without `name` throws `Error` naming the line number\n- [ ] A `color` that is not 6 hex digits throws `Error` naming the label\n- [ ] Duplicate label names throw `Error` listing both occurrences\n- [ ] Tests in `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs` cover the three cases\n- [ ] Error messages are clear and user-friendly"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B2 "Unmeasurable: should be faster": the last item has no threshold, the others are deterministic.
{"id":"invalid-partial-ac-unmeasurable","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac"],"input":{"title":"[PERF] Cache parsed prompts in loadPrompt","body":"`loadPrompt(name)` in `scripts/lib/prompts.mjs` reads the file on every call.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A second `loadPrompt('validation-system')` call does not call `fs.readFileSync` (asserted with a mock)\n- [ ] The cached value is identical to the first returned string\n- [ ] A missing file still throws `Prompt file not found`\n- [ ] Pipeline runs are noticeably faster"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B2 "Dependent on undefined human judgment": "réaliste" has no measurable definition; the other items are testable.
{"id":"invalid-fr-partial-ac","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac","fr"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Ajouter un résumé des coûts au rapport d'évals","body":"Ajouter une section `## Coût` au rapport Markdown produit par `scripts/lib/eval_harness.mjs`.\n\n## Critères d'acceptation\n- [ ] La section affiche `tokens_est` total et par cas\n- [ ] La section est absente quand `tokens_est` vaut 0\n- [ ] Un test dans `scripts/tests/eval_harness.test.mjs` vérifie les deux cas\n- [ ] L'estimation en dollars est réaliste"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B3 "scope boundary unclear (… all users or a specific role?)": endpoints are explicit, who may call PATCH/DELETE is not.
{"id":"invalid-role-ambiguous","tags":["invalid","b3","role-scope"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Project member management endpoints","body":"Add member management to the Express API in `src/routes/projects.mjs`.\n\n## Endpoints\n- `GET /api/projects/:id/members` — list members\n- `PATCH /api/projects/:id/members/:userId` — change a member's role\n- `DELETE /api/projects/:id/members/:userId` — remove a member\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GET` returns 200 with `[{ userId, role }]`\n- [ ] `PATCH` and `DELETE` return 403 for users who are not allowed to manage members\n- [ ] `DELETE` on an unknown member returns 404\n- [ ] Tests in `test/projects.test.mjs` cover each status code"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B3 "Key terms are undefined and could mean multiple incompatible things": "admins" maps to two existing roles.
{"id":"invalid-role-two-admin-roles","tags":["invalid","b3","role-scope"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Restrict audit log export to admins","body":"`GET /api/audit/export` in `src/routes/audit.mjs` is open to every authenticated user. The app has two admin roles today: `org_admin` and `project_admin` (scoped to one project).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Admins get 200 with a CSV body\n- [ ] Other authenticated users get 403\n- [ ] Anonymous requests get 401\n- [ ] Tests cover the three responses"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B3 "which environments?": "deployed environments" could mean staging+prod or every non-local env (preview included).
{"id":"invalid-scope-environment","tags":["invalid","b3"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Disable debug logging in deployed environments","body":"`LOG_LEVEL=debug` leaks request bodies. `config/env/` holds `local.yaml`, `preview.yaml`, `staging.yaml`, `production.yaml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `LOG_LEVEL` is `info` in every deployed environment\n- [ ] `local.yaml` keeps `LOG_LEVEL: debug`\n- [ ] `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs` asserts the level per file"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B4 "requires a service … that does not yet exist AND no documented workaround, stub, mock, or resolution plan" + contract assumed without citation.
{"id":"invalid-dependency-no-stub","tags":["invalid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Show model cost in the PR review comment","body":"`scripts/pr_review.mjs` should append the review's cost, fetched from the pricing service the platform team is starting. It has no endpoint yet; it will return `{ usd }` for a model and token count.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The review comment ends with `Cost: $<usd>` rounded to 4 decimals\n- [ ] When the pricing call fails, the line reads `Cost: n/a`\n- [ ] A test in `scripts/tests/pr_review.test.mjs` covers both lines"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// B1 "AC section exists but contains only vague statements" ("fix the bug", "should work correctly"), in French.
{"id":"invalid-fr-vague-ac","tags":["invalid","b1","fr"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] L'export CSV plante","body":"L'export CSV plante de temps en temps.\n\n## Critères d'acceptation\n- [ ] Corriger le bug\n- [ ] L'export doit fonctionner correctement"},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-short-no-ac","tags":["invalid","b1","short"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Clean up models config","body":"Tidy `config/models.yaml`."},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
// B4 NOT BLOCKED "in-progress (with ticket), or explicitly mocked/stubbed": both are present here.
{"id":"valid-dependency-ticket-stub","tags":["valid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Send review verdict to the notifier service","body":"The notifier service is in progress (PLAT-412, contract: `docs/contracts.md#notifier` — `POST /notify { prNumber, verdict }` → 202). Until it ships, `scripts/lib/notifier_stub.mjs` exports `notify()` that records calls in memory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/pr_review.mjs` calls `notify({ prNumber, verdict })` once per review\n- [ ] The notifier client is injected, so tests pass the stub\n- [ ] A `notify()` rejection is logged via `log({ level: 'error' })` and the review still completes\n- [ ] Tests in `scripts/tests/pr_review.test.mjs` cover success and rejection with the stub\n\n## Out of scope\nWiring the real client (follow-up once PLAT-412 is deployed)."},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
// B4 NOT BLOCKED "in-progress (with ticket)": a ticket with a cited contract is a resolution plan; no stub is required by the prompt.
{"id":"valid-dependency-ticket-no-stub","tags":["valid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Read model prices from the pricing service","body":"Add `getPrice(model)` to `scripts/lib/pricing.mjs`. The pricing service is in progress under PLAT-430 (staging ETA next sprint); its contract is published in `docs/contracts.md#pricing`: `GET /prices/:model` → 200 `{ inputPerMTok, outputPerMTok }`, 404 for an unknown model.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `getPrice('gpt-oss-120b')` returns `{ inputPerMTok, outputPerMTok }` from the response body\n- [ ] A 404 resolves to `null`\n- [ ] Any other status throws `Error` with the status code\n- [ ] Tests in `scripts/tests/pricing.test.mjs` mock `fetch` for the three cases"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-short","tags":["valid","short"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] formatDuration(0) returns NaN","body":"In `scripts/lib/metrics.mjs`.\n\n## AC\n- [ ] `formatDuration(0)` returns `'0s'`\n- [ ] Regression test in `scripts/tests/metrics.test.mjs`"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-fr-short","tags":["valid","fr","short"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] slugify garde les accents","body":"Dans `scripts/lib/strings.mjs`.\n\n## Critères d'acceptation\n- [ ] `slugify('Évaluation')` retourne `'evaluation'`\n- [ ] `slugify('')` retourne toujours `''`\n- [ ] Test ajouté dans `scripts/tests/strings.test.mjs`"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
